# The shell scripts must reach a Linux host with LF endings. A CRLF one
# fails on the first line with "$'\r': command not found" - a message that
# names no file and reads like a corrupted download rather than a line
# ending. This repo is authored on Windows, so without this the endings
# depend on whatever core.autocrlf each contributor happens to have set.
#
# The committed execute bit matters for the same reason and is recorded in
# the index (100755), not here - git has no attribute for it. Both are
# asserted by tests/test_dbcheck.py so neither can quietly regress.
*.sh text eol=lf
